From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:30:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] FMRadio: powerUp passes the frequency in 10 kHz units

MediaTek's FMR_pwr_up() checks the frequency against the band from the
vendor libfmcust (for example 8750..10800, in 10 kHz units), but the JNI
powerUp passed freq * 10, so every power-up failed with
"FMR_pwr_up error freq: 1000". Tune and seek are left alone: FMR_tune()
has no band check and the kernel accepts both units.
---
 jni/fmr/libfm_jni.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/jni/fmr/libfm_jni.cpp b/jni/fmr/libfm_jni.cpp
index a906887..2dfc1ca 100644
--- a/jni/fmr/libfm_jni.cpp
+++ b/jni/fmr/libfm_jni.cpp
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ jboolean powerUp(JNIEnv *env, jobject thiz, jfloat freq)
     int tmp_freq;
 
     LOGI("%s, [freq=%d]\n", __func__, (int)freq);
-    tmp_freq = (int)(freq * 10);        //Eg, 87.5 * 10 --> 875
+    tmp_freq = (int)(freq * 100);       //Eg, 87.5 * 100 --> 8750, the unit of the libfmcust band limits
     ret = FMR_pwr_up(g_idx, tmp_freq);
 
     LOGD("%s, [ret=%d]\n", __func__, ret);
